{"id": "cvnpcexqymnpkvj1l", "title": "Design a simple but scalable e...", "updated_at": "2026-04-08T08:35:20.630Z", "messages": [{"id": 1, "role": "ai", "text": "Hello! I am your AI architect powered by Llama3. Describe the system you want to build, or ask me to modify the current board."}, {"id": 1775624325421, "role": "user", "text": "Design a simple but scalable e-commerce system for handling ~3000 concurrent users using proper microservices architecture. Include API Gateway, core services (auth, product, cart, order, payment), databases, caching (Redis), and async processing (Kafka). Clearly show request flow, service-to-service communication, and avoid direct database access from the API Gateway"}, {"id": 1775624417217, "role": "ai", "text": "Here is the revised architecture on the board based on your prompt."}, {"id": 1775624497479, "role": "user", "text": "i need to implement the whatsapp chat  in the frontend"}, {"id": 1775624630048, "role": "ai", "text": "Here is the revised architecture on the board based on your prompt."}, {"id": 1775636121368, "role": "user", "text": "i need to add the push notification for the user too add that feature also into the design"}, {"id": 1775636204611, "role": "ai", "text": "So you want to integrate WhatsApp chat and push notifications into our e-commerce system. That's a great addition!\n\nFor WhatsApp integration, we'll need to consider how to handle incoming messages and updates from customers. I suggest adding a new microservice specifically for handling WhatsApp-related requests. This service can be responsible for processing incoming messages, updating customer records, and triggering relevant actions in other services (e.g., product updates).\n\nHere's a possible implementation:\n\n* Create a new microservice, let's call it `WhatsAppHandler`. This service will be responsible for receiving and processing WhatsApp messages.\n* `WhatsAppHandler` will need to communicate with the existing `Auth` service to verify the customer's identity and ensure they are authorized to interact with our e-commerce system.\n* When a customer sends a message through WhatsApp, the `WhatsAppHandler` microservice can update their record in the `Customer` service accordingly. For example, if a customer asks about product availability, the `WhatsAppHandler` can query the `Product` service and retrieve the relevant information.\n\nFor push notifications, we'll need to consider how to trigger notifications for specific events (e.g., order updates, price changes). I suggest adding a new microservice specifically for handling push notifications. This service can be responsible for sending push notifications to customers when certain events occur.\n\nHere's a possible implementation:\n\n* Create a new microservice, let's call it `PushNotification`. This service will be responsible for sending push notifications to customers.\n* The `PushNotification` microservice will need to communicate with the existing services (e.g., `Order`, `Product`) to retrieve relevant information and trigger notifications accordingly.\n* When an event occurs that requires a push notification (e.g., order update), the affected service can publish a message to a Kafka topic. The `PushNotification` microservice can then consume this message, generate the necessary notification, and send it to the customer.\n\nTo illustrate how these new services will interact with the existing architecture, I'll create a new version of our architecture board. Please let me know when you're ready!\n\n(Remember, you can always ask me questions or provide feedback before we finalize the design.)"}, {"id": 1775637232468, "role": "user", "text": "hi"}, {"id": 1775637255267, "role": "ai", "text": "Hi! It looks like we were in the middle of designing your e-commerce system with WhatsApp chat and push notifications. I was proposing adding two new microservices: `WhatsAppHandler` for handling incoming messages and updates, and `PushNotification` for sending notifications to customers. Would you like me to walk you through those proposals again or is there something specific you'd like to discuss?"}, {"id": 1775637291644, "role": "user", "text": "so im planning to add customer care support what do you think"}, {"id": 1775637318612, "role": "ai", "text": "Customer care support sounds like a great addition! I'm curious, are you thinking of integrating this with the WhatsAppHandler microservice we discussed earlier? Perhaps we could have a single point of contact for customer inquiries, where WhatsApp messages and phone calls can be handled together?\n\nWe might also need to consider how to route incoming customer requests (e.g., emails, chats) to the right team or agent. I'd suggest adding a new microservice specifically for handling customer care support, which can integrate with WhatsAppHandler and other services as needed.\n\nWhat are your thoughts on this?"}], "nodes": [{"id": "api-gateway", "data": {"label": "API Gateway"}, "type": "Microservice", "targetPosition": "top", "sourcePosition": "bottom", "position": {"x": 380, "y": 280}, "style": {"background": "#151618", "color": "#EDEEF0", "border": "1px solid #2C2D31", "borderRadius": "8px", "padding": "12px 16px", "fontSize": "13px", "fontWeight": "500", "boxShadow": "0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)", "width": "180px", "textAlign": "center", "letterSpacing": "0.01em", "borderTop": "3px solid #3B82F6"}, "measured": {"width": 180, "height": 47}, "selected": false, "dragging": false}, {"id": "auth-ms", "data": {"label": "Auth Microservice"}, "type": "Microservice", "targetPosition": "top", "sourcePosition": "bottom", "position": {"x": 1070, "y": 280}, "style": {"background": "#151618", "color": "#EDEEF0", "border": "1px solid #2C2D31", "borderRadius": "8px", "padding": "12px 16px", "fontSize": "13px", "fontWeight": "500", "boxShadow": "0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)", "width": "180px", "textAlign": "c